---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`} description="What this site stores. Almost nothing." path="/privacy">
  <main class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
      <h1>What is kept, and for how long</h1>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        A question you ask AI Aden is sent to the model provider (Anthropic by default) with the few turns before it, used to write the answer, and not stored by this site. There is no account and no transcript archive. A session cookie counts the live questions you have used today and expires after a day.
      </p>
      <h2>Messages</h2>
      <p>
        If you send Aden a message or a call request, the site stores what you typed (name, email, optional company, message) and the last few turns of the conversation, so he has the context. It is kept for 30 days and only Aden can read it. Nothing is sent anywhere automatically.
      </p>
      <h2>Limits and telemetry</h2>
      <p>
        Rate limits use the connecting IP. The daily spend is a single counter. Telemetry, when Cloudflare Analytics Engine is bound, records the cost of each answer and which path produced it. It does not record the text of your question.
      </p>
      <h2>Voice</h2>
      <p>
        When voice is enabled, the answer text is sent to ElevenLabs to synthesize audio, which is played once and not stored. The voice only ever speaks answers this site produced.
      </p>
      <p>If you would rather keep a model out of the loop, the static pages and <a href="/notes">the notes</a> have everything.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
